---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CardGrid from '../../../components/CardGrid.astro';
import DocCard from '../../../components/DocCard.astro';
const sidebar = [
  { title: 'Documentation Home', href: '/docs' },
  { title: 'Reference Overview', href: '/docs/reference', active: true },
  { title: 'Glossary', href: '/docs/reference/glossary' },
  { title: 'Known Issues', href: '/docs/reference/known-issues' },
  { title: 'Roadmap', href: '/docs/reference/roadmap' },
  { title: 'Changelog', href: '/docs/reference/changelog' },
  { title: 'Literature', href: '/docs/reference/literature' },
];
const toc = [
  { id: 'categories', text: 'Reference Categories', level: 2 },
  { id: 'architecture', text: 'Architecture Reference', level: 2 },
  { id: 'modules', text: 'Pure Modules', level: 2 },
  { id: 'honest', text: 'Honest Assessment', level: 2 },
];
---
<DocsLayout title="Reference" description="Reference materials for the honeypot system" section="Reference" sidebar={sidebar} toc={toc}>
  <h2 id="categories">Reference Categories</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <DocCard title="Glossary" href="/docs/reference/glossary" icon="book" tag="Definitions" description="Core concepts, detection terms, architecture terms, scoring terms and operations terms in one searchable page." meta="5 sections" />
    <DocCard title="Known Issues & Corrections" href="/docs/reference/known-issues" icon="alert" tag="Workarounds" description="Current issues, historical bugs that were fixed, and the correction process for documentation." meta="Severity + workaround" />
    <DocCard title="Roadmap" href="/docs/reference/roadmap" icon="route" tag="Planning" description="Near-, mid- and long-term work, including the deliberate choice to keep detection rule-based for now." meta="3 horizons" />
    <DocCard title="Changelog" href="/docs/reference/changelog" icon="clock" tag="History" description="Detection pipeline changes, routing and pooling work, and security fixes with the reasoning behind them." meta="Unreleased + historical" />
    <DocCard title="Primary Literature" href="/docs/reference/literature" icon="book" tag="Sources" description="Academic foundations, technical references for Suricata, AbuseIPDB and Kibana, and related work." meta="Academic + technical" />
    <DocCard title="Reference Hub" href="/reference" icon="search" tag="Quick lookup" description="A compact page of key terms and tables for when you do not want to read a full section." meta="One screen" />
  </CardGrid>

  <h2 id="architecture">Architecture Reference</h2>
  <p>The honeypot system is built on a layered architecture following a pure/adapter split pattern. All core logic lives in <code>*_rules.lua</code> modules with zero <code>ngx.*</code> dependencies, making them unit-testable under a plain Lua interpreter.</p>

  <h2 id="modules">Pure Modules</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Module</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    <tr><td>pattern_rules.lua</td><td>URI/header/CVE pattern scoring</td></tr>
    <tr><td>vulnerability_rules.lua</td><td>CVE/exploit-kit pattern matching</td></tr>
    <tr><td>suricata_rules.lua</td><td>eve.json alert parsing/scoring</td></tr>
    <tr><td>abuseipdb_rules.lua</td><td>Report eligibility logic</td></tr>
    <tr><td>router_rules.lua</td><td>Routing predicates</td></tr>
    <tr><td>upload_rules.lua</td><td>File-upload pattern analysis</td></tr>
    <tr><td>admin_rules.lua</td><td>Admin-access decision logic</td></tr>
    <tr><td>session_rules.lua</td><td>Session anomaly detection</td></tr>
    <tr><td>decay_policy.lua</td><td>Escalation-aware decay</td></tr>
    <tr><td>lua_pattern_utils.lua</td><td>Shared string helpers</td></tr>
    <tr><td>ip_rules.lua</td><td>IPv4/IPv6 CIDR matching</td></tr>
    <tr><td>honeytoken_rules.lua</td><td>Token-in-corpus matching</td></tr>
    <tr><td>gdpr_rules.lua</td><td>Consent-gated identity</td></tr>
    <tr><td>shared_ip_rules.lua</td><td>Shared-address policy</td></tr>
    <tr><td>pool_router_rules.lua</td><td>Pool routing logic</td></tr>
    <tr><td>session_identity_rules.lua</td><td>Session cookie identity</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2 id="honest">Honest Assessment</h2>
  <p><strong>Strengths:</strong> Comprehensive detection, explainable architecture, per-attacker isolation, privacy-preserving, full telemetry.</p>
  <p><strong>Limitations:</strong> Same-host testing gap, decay complexity, honeytoken coverage (5 types), no ML, Redis dependency, pool scaling limits, dashboard drift, no automated health monitoring.</p>
</DocsLayout>
